 "_comment": "H-1B provisions of the INA, as enforced by the DOL Wage and Hour Division. THIS IS A FLOOR, NEVER A RATE: these are violations FOUND, which requires a complaint or an investigation, so nothing here counts violations that occurred and a low figure is NOT evidence of compliance -- it is equally consistent with nobody complaining, which is what employer dependence would predict. BACK WAGES ARE 'AGREED TO PAY', a finding and an agreement, not money proven collected. Cases are dated by FINDINGS_END_DATE and an investigation can cover several earlier years. Employers are grouped on the filed legal name with case and whitespace normalised only -- nothing is fuzzy-matched, so two spellings of one company remain two rows and totals per company are a floor.",
